      <span class="tg-hero__type">Part I of Five</span>
      <h1 class="tg-hero__title">Text, Reception, and the Weight of Evidence</h1>
      <p class="tg-hero__intro">
        Before the passage can be applied it has to be read. This part sets out what
        Numbers 16–17 actually contains — two coalitions with unrelated grievances, two
        judgments, two signs, and a charter — then traces the composition debate, the
        reception history from Sirach to the English Civil War, and an honest accounting
        of which claims the evidence supports and which it does not.
      </p>
      <blockquote class="tg-hero__key-verse">
        <p>And Moses said to Korah, "In the morning the LORD will show who is his,
           and who is holy, and will bring him near to him."</p>
        <cite><a class="ref" data-ref="Numbers 16:5">Numbers 16:5</a></cite>
      </blockquote>
    </div>
